[
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like having a theorem stating <code>ptrEq a b → a = b</code> should be safe. At the very least, adding this as an axiom shouldn't be dangerous. I was expecting to find it in the standard distribution, but having search I at least couldn't find it. Am I correct in assuming I can just ask just assume this?</p>",
        "id": 617258856,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787072688
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The reason I would need something like this is to justify some meta code I'm writing. I have an invariant that says  that a function is only callable with a parameter which is the precise value of some other argument's field. The issue is that this parameter's type does not have a lawful <code>BEq</code>, but I feel I should be able to get away with comparing with <code>ptrEq</code>, and failing otherwise. So now I would just like a way to transform my <code>ptrEq a b</code> into <code>a = b</code> so I'm able to write the rest of the function</p>",
        "id": 617259862,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787072938
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nvm, <code>ptrEq</code> is not even a function, you can't reason about it</p>",
        "id": 617260779,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787073186
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ptrEq#doc\">docs#ptrEq</a> is unsafe, so any theorem about it must also be unsafe</p>",
        "id": 617260844,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787073208
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can of course write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">defProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq_of_ptrEq_eq_true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptrEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lcProof</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617260867,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787073215
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm</p>",
        "id": 617260895,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787073225
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like this theorem shouldn't really be <code>unsafe</code>, however</p>",
        "id": 617261107,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787073301
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It feels a bit like a partial correctness property</p>",
        "id": 617261170,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787073315
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Keep in mind that this is true:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptrEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- true</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617264319,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1787074156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oooh. How come?</p>",
        "id": 617264396,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787074178
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Types are erased at runtime, so <code>True</code> and <code>False</code> are both represented by a null pointer.</p>",
        "id": 617264573,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1787074218
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, yes, I was reading those wrong. That makes sense. It's definitely an unsafe operation then</p>",
        "id": 617264741,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787074254
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess what I really want is <code>a == b → a = b</code> for <code>Lean.Expr</code> and <code>Lean.Level</code>, which is what's making my type not have a lawful equality</p>",
        "id": 617264969,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787074299
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also not true :-)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LawfulBEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">native_decide</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Well but <code>Level</code> does have <code>LawfulBEq</code> and you can't prove it, that's right.</p>",
        "id": 617270566,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1787075617
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wait, but what's the use of having alpha conversion in Eq's <code>BEq</code>?</p>",
        "id": 617271076,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787075715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Like, there's no reason why <code>Expr</code> should not have decidable equality, right?</p>",
        "id": 617271395,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787075789
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"690100\">Fernando LEAL</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/ptrEq.20implies.20Eq.3F.20.28no.2C.20ptrEq.20is.20unsafe.29/near/617261107\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I feel like this theorem shouldn't really be <code>unsafe</code>, however</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Theorems about <code>unsafe</code> definitions are foced by the compiler to themselves be unsafe</p>",
        "id": 617271541,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787075822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"690100\">Fernando LEAL</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/ptrEq.20implies.20Eq.3F.20.28no.2C.20ptrEq.20is.20unsafe.29/near/617271076\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wait, but what's the use of having alpha conversion in Eq's <code>BEq</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It helps with e.g. having Expr based caches be more aggressive</p>",
        "id": 617271615,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1787075838
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"395550\">Henrik Böving</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/ptrEq.20implies.20Eq.3F.20.28no.2C.20ptrEq.20is.20unsafe.29/near/617271615\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It helps with e.g. having Expr based caches be more aggressive</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>But this is only true because  <code>Std.HashMap</code> (or persistent or whatever) requires this comparison to be <code>BEq</code></p>",
        "id": 617272285,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787075999
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Idk, I understand that my usecase is clearly much more uncommon than I thought. I'm just surprised by the default behaviour a little</p>",
        "id": 617272506,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1787076037
    }
]